{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Also</b> — the poetic form יחשיך is defective; nothing is hidden from You." "<b>And the word as darkness, so light</b> — a concise construction, like כעבד כאדוניו, כעמי כעמך. The sense is עמי כעמך and עמך כעמי — there is no difference between them."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 139, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:42:10.649693862Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}